{"paper": "RRB-RPF-Constable-04-Mar-2025-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": false, "extracted_count": 120, "tagged_count": 34, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "After 60 litres of petrol was poured into an empty storage tank, it was still 10% empty. How much petrol (in litres, rounded off to two decimal place) must be poured into the storage tank in order to fill it?", "options": [{"text": "67.67", "added": false}, {"text": "65.67", "added": false}, {"text": "61", "added": false}, {"text": "66.67", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "fill-empty", "key_answer": "66.67"}, {"n": 2, "text": "If the selling price of 10 raincoats is equal to the cost price of 12 raincoats, find the gain percentage.", "options": [{"text": "12%", "added": false}, {"text": "15%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "16%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": "20%"}, {"n": 3, "text": "Find the value of 8.15 × 0.35 − 2.36 × 0.8 + 1.07 − 0.5 × 0.8 − 2.56.", "options": [{"text": "−0.6354", "added": false}, {"text": "−0.4356", "added": false}, {"text": "−0.2235", "added": false}, {"text": "−0.9255", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "−0.9255"}, {"n": 4, "text": "Jitesh and Kamal can complete a certain piece of work in 7 and 11 days, respectively, They started to work together, and after 3 days, Kamal left. In how many days will Jitesh complete the remaining work?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "Two banks, A and B, offered loans at 3.5% and 6% per annum, respectively. Ajay borrowed an amount of ₹340000 from each bank. Find the positive difference between the amounts of simple interest paid to the two banks by Ajay after 3 years.", "options": [{"text": "25500", "added": false}, {"text": "27000", "added": false}, {"text": "26500", "added": false}, {"text": "25000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": "25500"}, {"n": 6, "text": "Anwesha sells two handbags, one at a profit of 18% and the other at a loss of 18%. If the selling price of each handbag is ₹450, then what is the overall percentage of profit or loss?", "options": [{"text": "3.24% profit", "added": false}, {"text": "2.34% profit", "added": false}, {"text": "3.24% loss", "added": false}, {"text": "2.34% loss", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": "3.24% loss"}, {"n": 7, "text": "Mohan bought 52 books for Rs 1130 from one shop and 44 books for Rs 920 from another. What is the average price (in Rs) he paid per book ?", "options": [{"text": "1033.75", "added": false}, {"text": "1023.75", "added": false}, {"text": "1043.75", "added": false}, {"text": "1048.75", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "1033.75"}, {"n": 8, "text": "Find the difference between the simple interest and compound interest, compounded annually, on an amount of ₹35,000 at 12% for 3 years.", "options": [{"text": "₹1,527.48", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,572.48", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,725.84", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,752.84", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "si-ci-difference", "key_answer": "₹1,572.48"}, {"n": 9, "text": "Evaluate: 2 × {17 - 2 × (8 -6)}", "options": [{"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "26", "added": false}, {"text": "23", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topi